  "description": "##Rear T1 Lime x 1 (Tilia spp) 18m mature lime, cyclical prune - canopy overhangs several neighbouring gardens and is encroaching upon the rear neighbours roof. Suggested work: - crown reduction - remove basal growth - lift canopy to 8m by removing trunk epicormic growth - reduce the canopy height 3m back to previous reduction points - reduce the lateral growth 2-2.5m back to previous reduction points, leaving furnishing growth ##Rear T2 Holly x 1 (Ilex aquifolium) 5m holly tree is impeding the residents access to the garden as it is encroaching upon the stairs to the garden. Suggested work: - lift to 2m, removing basal growth - reduce height 1.5m and trim remaining canopy into conical shape",
